# Railway Environment Variables Template
# Copy this to your Railway service environment variables

# ===== DATABASE CONFIGURATION =====
# Railway automatically provides DATABASE_URL when you add PostgreSQL
# You MUST manually set these to use the PostgreSQL database:
# (Do NOT use ${DATABASE_URL} syntax - Railway doesn't expand it)
# 
# In Railway dashboard, set these variables to: $DATABASE_URL
# (Railway will automatically substitute this at runtime)
DWN_TTL_CACHE_URL=$DATABASE_URL
DWN_STORAGE_MESSAGES=$DATABASE_URL
DWN_STORAGE_DATA=$DATABASE_URL
DWN_STORAGE_EVENTS=$DATABASE_URL
DWN_STORAGE_RESUMABLE_TASKS=$DATABASE_URL

# ===== SERVER CONFIGURATION =====
# Railway automatically provides PORT, but DWN server uses DS_PORT
DS_PORT=$PORT
# Update this to your actual Railway domain
DWN_BASE_URL=https://your-service-name.railway.app

# ===== DISABLE TENANT REGISTRATION (for open server) =====
# Don't set DWN_REGISTRATION_STORE_URL to keep registration disabled
# Don't set DWN_STORAGE to avoid registration fallback

# ===== OPTIONAL CONFIGURATION =====
# Uncomment and configure as needed:

# Enable WebSocket support
DWN_WS_PORT=3001
DS_WEBSOCKET_SERVER=on

# Set custom data size limit (default: 1gb)
MAX_RECORD_DATA_SIZE=1gb

# Enable debug logging (useful for debugging Railway deployments)
# DWN_SERVER_LOG_LEVEL=debug

# Terms of service (if required)
# DWN_TERMS_OF_SERVICE_FILE_PATH=/app/terms-of-service.txt

# ===== RAILWAY-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION =====
# Railway provides these automatically:
# DATABASE_URL - PostgreSQL connection string
# PORT - The port Railway expects your app to listen on
# RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT - The environment name (production, staging, etc.)
# RAILWAY_SERVICE_NAME - Your service name
# RAILWAY_PROJECT_NAME - Your project name